From faf83d1cf89d7c44c12e3e7b79ff271d778a609d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: TrinityXSX <trinityxsx@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 13:20:27 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] TrinityXSX: Web Companion session cookie instead of the PIN
 in URLs

Every link, form, fetch and redirect carried ?pin=NNNNNN, so the PIN
stayed in browser history, the address bar and anything that logs URLs.

- The QR code still logs in with one scan: a GET with the right PIN
  gets a 303 to the same URL without it and a session cookie
  (txsx_session, 128-bit, HttpOnly, SameSite=Lax; Lax so a QR opened
  from the camera app keeps it on the redirect). All GET routes are
  read-only.
- The dashboard HTML and script no longer contain the PIN.
- POSTs whose Origin is not this server are refused (403), so another
  website cannot submit the dashboard's forms with the cookie.
- The dashboard notice (?msg=) is shown only for this site's own
  navigations (Sec-Fetch-Site), so a link from elsewhere cannot put
  its own text in the real dashboard.
- Without a session or PIN, paths other than / answer 401; the log
  viewer and save restore stop and ask to scan the QR again (e.g. a
  tab from before a restart, which also gets a new token).
